      "text": "To determine how many minutes it will take to print 200 pages, we start by noting the printer's printing speed, which is 17 pages per minute. We need to find out how many minutes \\( t \\) it will take to print 200 pages.\n\nThe relationship between the total number of pages printed, the speed of the printer, and the time taken is given by the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{Total pages} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time}\n\\]\nSubstituting the known values into the formula, we get:\n\\[\n200 = 17 \\times t\n\\]\nTo solve for \\( t \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 17:\n\\[\nt = \\frac{200}{17}\n\\]\nPerforming the division, we find:\n\\[\nt \\approx 11.7647\n\\]\nSince the problem asks for the time to the nearest whole number, we round 11.7647 to the nearest whole number, which is 12. Therefore, the time it will take to print 200 pages is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]",
