      "text": "To determine how many minutes it will take to print 200 pages, we start with the given print rate and the total number of pages to be printed.\n\nThe printer prints at a rate of 17 pages per minute. We need to find out how many minutes, \\( t \\), it will take to print 200 pages. We can set up the following equation based on the relationship between the rate, time, and the total number of pages:\n\n\\[ \\text{Rate} \\times \\text{Time} = \\text{Total Pages} \\]\n\\[ 17 \\, \\text{pages/minute} \\times t \\, \\text{minutes} = 200 \\, \\text{pages} \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( t \\), we rearrange the equation to isolate \\( t \\):\n\n\\[ t = \\frac{200 \\, \\text{pages}}{17 \\, \\text{pages/minute}} \\]\n\nNow, we perform the division:\n\n\\[ t \\approx \\frac{200}{17} \\approx 11.7647 \\]\n\nRounding 11.7647 to the nearest whole number, we get:\n\n\\[ t \\approx 12 \\]\n\nTherefore, it will take approximately \\(\\boxed{12}\\) minutes to print 200 pages.",
