      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine how long it takes for the printer to print 200 pages given that the printer prints at a rate of 17 pages per minute.\n\nFirst, let's denote the time it takes to print 200 pages as \\( t \\) minutes. The relationship between the number of pages printed, the rate of printing, and the time can be expressed with the equation:\n\\[\n\\text{Rate} \\times \\text{Time} = \\text{Number of Pages}\n\\]\nHere, the rate of printing is 17 pages per minute, and the number of pages printed is 200. So we can write:\n\\[\n17 \\times t = 200\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( t \\), we need to solve the equation for \\( t \\):\n\\[\nt = \\frac{200}{17}\n\\]\n\nNext, we perform the division to find the value of \\( t \\):\n\\[\nt \\approx \\frac{200}{17} \\approx 11.7647\n\\]\n\nSince the problem asks for the time to the nearest whole number, we round 11.7647 to the nearest whole number, which is 12.\n\nTherefore, the time it takes to print 200 pages is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]",
